    // As argued in the original code, B[k][j] is always read from the
    // original B (no in-place dependence across rows), so we can write:
    //
    //   B_out[i][j] = alpha * ( B_in[i][j] +
    //                           sum_{k = i+1..M-1} A[k][i] * B_in[k][j] )
    //
    // Mapping indices to Halide (buffer coordinates are (x = column, y = row)):
    //   A[k][i]  -> A_param(i, k)   (x = i, y = k)
    //   B[k][j]  -> B_param(j, k)   (x = j, y = k)
    //   B[i][j]  -> B_param(j, i)   (x = j, y = i)
